  <h2>The kitchen is where your home actually happens.</h2>
  <p>
    It’s where your family lands at the end of the day and where every party somehow ends up. When
    it’s dated, cramped, or just doesn’t flow, you feel it every single morning. A good kitchen
    remodel fixes that — but only if it’s planned around <em>your</em> life instead of a showroom
    catalog.
  </p>
  <p>
    That’s how we approach every kitchen at Reliable Builders. Before we talk tile or cabinet doors,
    we talk about how you cook, where things pile up, and what drives you crazy about the current
    space. Then we design around the answers.
  </p>
  <h3>Where a lot of kitchen remodels go wrong</h3>
  <p>
    Most kitchen headaches don’t come from bad taste — they come from bad process. A contractor
    lowballs the estimate to win the job, then the “surprises” start. Or the layout looks great on
    paper but the fridge door hits the island. Or the tile installer rushes and you’re staring at
    crooked grout lines for the next fifteen years.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do this differently on purpose. You get an honest number up front, a real designer helping
    with selections, and tile and stone work done by our own hands — not the cheapest sub we could
    find that week.
  </p>
  <h3>What your investment gets you</h3>
  <p>
    A well-built San Diego kitchen in the <strong>$30K–$60K</strong> range typically means new
    cabinetry, stone counters, a tile backsplash, updated lighting and electrical, and either a
    refreshed or reworked layout. We’ll show you exactly where your dollars go — and where a smart
    choice can save you a few thousand without anyone noticing the difference.
  </p>
